Link with \fI-lexpanse\fR.
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBexpanse_strmap_t\fR is an ordered dynamic radix trie mapping null-terminated
C strings (\fBconst char *\fR) to 64-bit integer values (\fBuint64_t\fR),
representing a modernized, clean-room equivalent of JudySL.
.PP
Keys are sorted in unsigned byte-lexicographical order.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <inttypes.h>
#include <expanse.h>

int main(void) {
    expanse_strmap_t *map = expanse_strmap_new();

    expanse_strmap_insert(map, "apple", 100, NULL);
    expanse_strmap_insert(map, "banana", 200, NULL);
    expanse_strmap_insert(map, "cherry", 300, NULL);

    /* Point query */
    uint64_t val;
    if (expanse_strmap_get(map, "banana", &val)) {
        printf("banana -> %" PRIu64 "\\n", val);
    }

    /* Truncation-safe ordered traversal */
    char buf[128];
    size_t req;
    expanse_str_nav_status st =
        expanse_strmap_first_ex(map, buf, sizeof(buf), &req, &val);

    while (st == EXPANSE_STR_NAV_OK) {
        printf("  %s => %" PRIu64 "\\n", buf, val);
        st = expanse_strmap_next_after_ex(map, buf, buf, sizeof(buf),
                                          &req, &val);
    }

    expanse_strmap_free(map);
    return 0;
}
.fi
.SH TRUNCATION-AWARE NAVIGATION
Classic string navigation functions (\fBexpanse_strmap_first\fR, etc.) return
\fBfalse\fR both when no key matches and when \fIbuf_len\fR is too small.
The \fB_ex\fR variants return an explicit \fBexpanse_str_nav_status\fR:
.TP
.B EXPANSE_STR_NAV_OK (0)
Success. The null-terminated key is written to \fIkey_out\fR.
.TP
.B EXPANSE_STR_NAV_NOT_FOUND (1)
No matching key found.
.TP
.B EXPANSE_STR_NAV_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL (2)
A matching key was found, but \fIbuf_len\fR was insufficient.
The exact required buffer size is reported in \fIrequired_len\fR.
